  "limits": [
    "Only the frozen skip-true B1 signatures have a full census here. The six ordinary requests lack writer, alias, compiled-cache and per-generation timing records. The half-savings scenario is a sensitivity, not a measured 13-job duration. Estimates assume at most one group per active target graph, using B4 native caller savings; a shortfall in hit rate, effective savings per call or critical-path exposure reduces the estimates. Paired stock metrics include one real request per engine and have distinct output-acceptance counts.",
